---
// Privacy Policy — real page (replaces the old /privacy static HTML).
// Built on the new Base layout so it inherits the theme, fonts, and tokens.
// Legal substance carried over from the prior policy and modernised to the
// Blak / Persona / Minit / Nexus / Learning naming, aligned with the landing's
// promises (yours · never sold · anonymous by default · you control memory).
// NOTE: not legal advice — have counsel review before relying on it. The
// effective date and contact email below are placeholders to confirm.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const effective = 'June 2, 2026';
const contact = 'ceo@blaksyd.com';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — Blaksyd"
  description="How Blaksyd collects, uses, and protects your data. Your world stays yours — never sold."
>
  <main class="legal">
    <header class="legal-head">
      <a href="/" class="legal-brand" aria-label="Blaksyd — home">
        <span class="bm" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </a>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-meta">Effective {effective} · Blaksyd LLP · blakcide.com &amp; blaksyd.com</p>
    </header>

    <article class="legal-body">
      <p class="lede">
        Blaksyd LLP (“Blaksyd”, “we”, “us”, “our”) respects your privacy. This policy
        explains how personal data is collected, used, stored, shared, and protected
        across blakcide.com, blaksyd.com, and the Blak, Persona, Minit, Nexus, and
        Learning services. The short version: <b>your world stays yours, and we never
        sell your personal data.</b>
      </p>

      <section>
        <h2>1. Data we collect</h2>
        <p>We may collect:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Account information (name, email, phone, username, and authentication credentials);</li>
          <li>Profile information you choose to add;</li>
          <li>Content you create — including messages, chats, journal entries, prompts, and the material your Persona is permitted to learn from;</li>
          <li>Technical and device data — IP address, browser/device identifiers, logs, and limited usage analytics;</li>
          <li>Payment-related information, only if paid features are introduced later;</li>
          <li>Support and verification records, where necessary.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>2. The sensitive nature of what you share</h2>
        <p>
          Blak, Minit, and Nexus are built for honest, emotionally real moments. Please
          avoid sharing highly confidential financial, medical, legal, or biometric
          details unless a feature expressly supports it and it is necessary.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>3. How we use data</h2>
        <p>We use data to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Provide and operate the services;</li>
          <li>Authenticate you and keep your account secure;</li>
          <li>Generate AI responses (Blak, Persona) and connect you with human listeners (Minit) and rooms (Nexus);</li>
          <li>Power your personal Learning engine — so the experience becomes more yours over time, never to sell you;</li>
          <li>Maintain safety, moderation, and abuse prevention;</li>
          <li>Improve quality, provide support, and meet legal obligations.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>4. Your control over memory</h2>
        <p>
          Persona only carries forward what you allow. You decide what it remembers and
          what it never repeats, and you can review, change, or delete that memory.
          Nexus is anonymous by default — you choose when, and whether, to be known.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>5. Legal basis</h2>
        <p>
          Where required, we rely on your consent, your instructions, contractual
          necessity, compliance obligations, and other lawful bases recognised under
          applicable Indian law.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>6. Children and age threshold</h2>
        <p>
          The services are intended for users <b>13 years and above</b>. Where a user is
          below the age of majority, parental or guardian involvement may be required by
          law. We do not knowingly allow the unlawful collection of children’s data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>7. Sharing of data</h2>
        <p>We may share data with:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Cloud and infrastructure providers acting on our behalf;</li>
          <li>Analytics, hosting, communication, payment, or security partners;</li>
          <li>Legal or regulatory authorities when genuinely required;</li>
          <li>Advisors in connection with compliance or disputes;</li>
          <li>An acquirer or successor in a merger, restructuring, or business transfer.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="callout"><b>We do not sell your personal data.</b> This is a commitment, not a placeholder.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>8. Retention</h2>
        <p>
          We retain data for as long as reasonably necessary to deliver the services and
          to meet safety, dispute-handling, fraud-prevention, and legal obligations — and
          no longer, unless the law requires it. You can request deletion at any time.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>9. Security</h2>
        <p>
          We use reasonable technical and organisational safeguards, and the site is
          served over HTTPS with strict security headers. No system is ever perfectly
          secure, and internet transmission carries inherent risk.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>10. Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Subject to applicable law, you may request access, correction, deletion, a copy
          of your data, or withdrawal of consent, and you may raise a grievance. Use the
          contact below.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>11. Cross-border processing</h2>
        <p>
          Data may be processed or stored in India or other jurisdictions through our
          service providers, subject to applicable legal safeguards and our controls.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>12. Cookies and analytics</h2>
        <p>
          This landing site itself sets <b>no advertising or cross-site tracking cookies</b>.
          It stores only your theme preference (dark/light) locally in your browser. Within
          the signed-in product we may use cookies and limited analytics to operate, secure,
          and improve the services; you can control some of these via your browser settings.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>13. Third-party links</h2>
        <p>
          Our platform may link to or integrate third-party tools. We are not responsible
          for their privacy practices — please review their policies.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>14. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For any privacy question or request, contact <b>Blaksyd LLP</b> at
          <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>15. Updates</h2>
        <p>
          We may revise this policy from time to time by posting an updated version with a
          new effective date.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>

    <a href="/" class="legal-back">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M19 12H5M11 18l-6-6 6-6" /></svg>
      Back to Blaksyd
    </a>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 760px; margin-inline: auto;
    padding: clamp(5.5rem, 12vh, 8rem) clamp(1.25rem, 5vw, 2rem) clamp(4rem, 9vh, 6rem);
    position: relative; z-index: 1;
  }

  .legal-head { text-align: center; margin-bottom: clamp(2.4rem, 5vh, 3.6rem); }
  .legal-brand { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; transition: transform var(--t-fast) var(--ease-spring); }
  .legal-brand:hover { transform: scale(1.04); }
  /* one wordmark fetched per theme (CSS background — inactive theme never downloaded) */
  .bm {
    display: block; height: 28px; width: auto; aspect-ratio: 737 / 338;
    background: url('/assets/blaksyd-white.webp') center / contain no-repeat;
  }
  html[data-theme="light"] .bm {
    aspect-ratio: 758 / 329;
    background-image: url('/assets/blaksyd-black.webp');
  }

  .legal-head h1 {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 1.4rem + 2.4vw, 3rem); letter-spacing: -.03em; color: var(--ink);
  }
  .legal-meta {
    margin-top: .9rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .7rem;
    text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .14em; color: var(--ink-faint);
  }

  .legal-body { color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .legal-body .lede {
    font-size: 1.12rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--ink);
    padding-bottom: 1.8rem; margin-bottom: .6rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .legal-body .lede b { font-weight: 600; }
  .legal-body section { margin-top: 2.1rem; }
  .legal-body h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.15rem; letter-spacing: -.01em; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: .7rem;
  }
  .legal-body p { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: .8rem; }
  .legal-body b { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
  .legal-body ul { list-style: none; margin: .2rem 0 1rem; display: grid; gap: .55rem; }
  .legal-body li {
    position: relative; padding-left: 1.4rem; font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .legal-body li::before {
    content: ''; position: absolute; left: .15rem; top: .62em;
    width: 6px; height: 6px; border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent-grad);
  }
  .legal-body a { color: var(--coral); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  .legal-body a:hover { color: var(--coral-deep, var(--coral)); }

  .legal-body .callout {
    margin-top: 1rem; padding: .9rem 1.1rem; border-radius: var(--r-md);
    background: var(--surface-strong); border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .legal-back {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .5rem;
    margin-top: clamp(3rem, 7vh, 4.5rem);
    font-size: .95rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink-soft);
    transition: color var(--t-fast) var(--ease-out), gap var(--t-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }
  .legal-back:hover { color: var(--ink); gap: .75rem; }
  .legal-back svg {
    width: 18px; height: 18px; fill: none; stroke: currentColor; stroke-width: 2;
    stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round;
  }
</style>
